# Секреты сервера. Скопируй в /srv/claude-api/data/server.env, chmod 600 (вне репо).
# Ключи НАШЕГО API через запятую. Клиент шлёт: x-api-key: <key>  (или Authorization: Bearer <key>).
# ПУСТО/нет файла — сервер принимает запросы ТОЛЬКО с 127.0.0.1.
CLAUDE_API_KEYS=put-a-long-random-key-here,another-key-for-second-client
# Read-only operational endpoints (/capacity, /metrics); production provisioning generates this.
CLAUDE_API_PANEL_KEY=put-a-separate-long-random-read-only-key-here
# Watchdog installer creates these once in production. Use independent random 64-hex values.
# Never add AUTH_BOT_PROXY_ADMIN_KEY or AUTH_BOT_PROXY_ADMIN_KEY_FILE here: provisioning rejects
# both settings. The canonical proxy-admin secret is the root-owned, non-deploy-writable
# /etc/apitoken/proxy-admin.key; LoadCredential copies it for authbot, whose ExecStart pins the copy path.
CLAUDE_API_REDIS_PASSWORD=replace-with-64-hex-redis-password
# Codex response history. Keeps 6379 because that instance already holds stored conversations.
CLAUDE_API_REDIS_URL=redis://default:replace-with-64-hex-redis-password@127.0.0.1:6379/0
# Cache affinity. A separate instance: maxmemory/maxmemory-policy are per-instance in Redis, so a
# shared one cannot give the two consumers independent budgets. Absent here, the engine falls back
# to CLAUDE_API_REDIS_URL, which is worse than a split but better than losing the L2 silently.
CLAUDE_API_AFFINITY_REDIS_URL=redis://default:replace-with-64-hex-redis-password@127.0.0.1:6380/0
CLAUDE_API_AFFINITY_SECRET=put-an-independent-64-random-hex-secret-here
# Optional last-resort ClaudeStore credential. Keep the switch in config.env disabled until the
# exact binary SHA is green and the authenticated smoke in docs/engine/CLAUDESTORE_FALLBACK.md passes.
# Never commit or print the real value; rotate any key that has crossed a chat or shell history.
# CLAUDE_API_CLAUDESTORE_API_KEY=put-the-root-owned-sk-cs4-key-here
# GPT fallback requires a different universal key switched to the ClaudeStore Codex tier. Never
# reuse the Basic/Claude key above. Provision only after the GPT live gate in the same runbook.
# CLAUDE_API_CLAUDESTORE_CODEX_API_KEY=put-the-root-owned-codex-tier-sk-cs4-key-here
# The private GPT Image 2 canary reuses the configured sealed Codex OAuth roster and keyring.
# There is deliberately no image-specific key, origin, or environment variable to provision.
# Optional KIMI plane keyring opening the AEAD credential envelopes (kid:64-hex[,...]). The same
# keyring authbot seals with; the plane ships default-off, so provision it only together with the
# reviewed unit change that enables the provider (docs/engine/KIMI_PROVIDER.md).
# CLAUDE_API_KIMI_CREDENTIAL_KEYS=current:<64-hex>[,old:<64-hex>]
